Before W32A-15, exactly ONE 7zFM import fell through to a loud TODO stub:
USER32!LoadBitmapW.  The pinned 7zFM.exe hits it on its first paint, when it
loads its toolbar bitmap strips — a real boot printed:

    w32run: /fat/7ZFM.EXE mapped at 0x400000000000, 292 import(s) bound
    w32: TODO user32.dll!LoadBitmapW needs W32A-5 (not yet implemented)

W32A-15 lands LoadBitmapW as REAL (w32/src/w32_rsrc.c + w32/src/w32_gdi.c):
RT_BITMAP resource -> device HBITMAP, expanding the 4bpp/16-colour toolbar
strips (and the 1bpp marker glyph) through their palette into native 32bpp.
LoadImageW's IMAGE_BITMAP path routes through the same helper.  After the fix
the same boot no longer prints the TODO line, and 7zFM's entire static surface
binds to an honest body.  Re-probed live:

    w32run: /fat/7ZFM.EXE mapped at 0x400000000000, 292 import(s) bound
    w32: advapi32!LsaOpenPolicy: refused -- no LSA database (STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED)
    w32: advapi32!OpenProcessToken: refused -- no token (ERROR_NO_TOKEN)
    w32: [shell32] SHGetFileInfoW: PIDL addressing is section 7 (ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER)
    (no LoadBitmapW TODO; no fault)

--- the security set stays fail-clean per the ledger (documented non-goals) ---
  ADVAPI32 (15 of 21 on 7zFM): AdjustTokenPrivileges, GetFileSecurityW,
  LookupAccountNameW, LookupPrivilegeValueW, the Lsa* family, OpenProcessToken,
  SetFileSecurityW — a single-user machine with no LSA/token database.  7-Zip's
  ACL-carrying archives extract with AuraLite's documented owner-only mapping;
  the casualty is named here and in the #7zip receipt, not hidden.
  MPR (6, delay): WNet* fail clean — no network provider (a documented non-goal).

